Confirms: in the real call order, load_necessary_databases() (called
by load_input_file BEFORE the input file's statements are exec'd)
constructs the global database first (in its except DatabaseError:
branch), so get_db() no longer raises by the time the input file's
own database(...) directive runs. The `or RMGDatabase()` at
arkane/input.py:111 is reached in this ordering, but vacuously --
get_db() already returns a truthy object, so RMGDatabase() (the
right-hand side) is never evaluated. Net: line 111's OWN
RMGDatabase() branch is unreachable in normal Arkane usage; not
because it doesn't need to be (get_db() truly can raise), but
because load_necessary_databases() -- a different construction
site -- always runs first and prevents get_db() from raising.
